// Title: CMSTP Execution Process Creation
// Sigma ID: 7d4cdc5a-0076-40ca-aac8-f7e714570e47
// Status: stable | Level: high
// Author: Nik Seetharaman
// Date: 2018-07-16 | Modified: 2020-12-23
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218.003, G0069
// Tags: car.2019-04-001
// Description: Detects various indicators of Microsoft Connection Manager Profile Installer execution
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate CMSTP use (unlikely in modern enterprise environments)
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20190720093911/http://www.endurant.io/cmstp/detecting-cmstp-enabled-code-execution-and-uac-bypass-with-sysmon/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmstp_execution_by_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmstp.exe"
